        ["R²", "0.9183", "0.9201"],
      ]
    ),
    spacer(80),
    ...figure('xgbActvsPred', "Figure 10: XGBoost — Actual vs. Predicted weekly sales. The scatter is tighter than Linear Regression but slightly wider than Random Forest, particularly at high sales magnitudes. R² = 0.9201 confirms strong predictive capacity."),
    spacer(80),
    ...figure('xgbResiduals', "Figure 11: XGBoost residual diagnostics. The residual distribution is approximately normal and centered near zero, with less structured pattern than Linear Regression, indicating a better-calibrated model."),
    spacer(80),
    ...figure('xgbFeatImp', "Figure 12: XGBoost feature importance (top 20). The distribution mirrors the Random Forest ranking: Size and department dummies dominate. XGBoost assigns slightly more importance to economic features than RF, likely due to sequential correction of residuals."),
    spacer(120),
    h2("4.6 Four-Model Comparison"),
    spacer(60),
    metricsTable(
      ["Metric", "Norm RF", "Raw RF", "Linear Reg", "XGBoost"],
      [
        ["MAE ($)", "$2,653.58", "$2,653.04", "$7,981.93", "$3,908.41"],
